<title>USA: HSBC Holdings unit sets $300 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>HSBC Holdings unit sets $300 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from HSBC Americas Inc was priced on Tuesday, via joint lead managers HSBC and Merrill Lynch &amp; Co, according to market sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER HSBC AMERICAS INC</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 11/01/2006</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES    ISS PRICE 99.16   FIRST PAY DATE 05/01/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY BAA1   YIELD 7.119 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS  SPREAD +72 BP     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212-859-1678</p>
